# Commercial S8.2 public activation helper precheck failure

Status: FAIL-CLOSED; NO SERVER MUTATION

The first public-activation helper attempt stopped at its first Git provenance
check. Its temporary `safe_git` wrapper passed `HEAD` as a Git subcommand
instead of running `git rev-parse HEAD`. Git returned:

`git: 'HEAD' is not a git command.`

This occurred before backup creation, nginx installation, database control
changes, unit enablement or nginx reload. Read-only post-state verification
proved:

- active nginx file SHA-256 remained
  `ddf14f890cf9d991b631371102663e8984f9586e3a2ee2afb7dace3b30a27843`
- nginx remained active with zero restarts
- S7 remained active with its prior PID and zero restarts
- S8 bot and landing remained active staging processes with zero restarts
- S8 bot, landing and health timer remained disabled
- the temporary helper removed itself

The corrected implementation is now versioned as
`scripts/tu1nz_adult_public_s8_activate_proxy.sh`. Its `git_value` helper uses
`git rev-parse`, it creates and verifies the full versioned S8 backup before
the authorized nginx write, and its post-backup failure path closes the
database kill switch, disables S8, restores the exact saved nginx file, reloads
nginx and revalidates S7. The previously verified S8.2 recovery backup remains
an additional rollback anchor.
